---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { url } from '../config/site';

const movedTools = [
  { name: 'Redis', desc: 'Browse and edit keys, view server info, run raw commands.' },
  { name: 'RabbitMQ', desc: 'Queues and exchanges, peek and publish messages, bindings, cluster overview.' },
  { name: 'Container Manager', desc: 'Containers, images, volumes, and networks on any Docker-compatible runtime.' },
  { name: 'Kafka Explorer', desc: 'Topics, partitions and offsets, consumer groups, producing messages.' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Plugin migration — DevTool"
  description="Redis, RabbitMQ, Container Manager, and Kafka Explorer are now optional plugins. What changed and how to get them back."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-14 pb-20">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
      Redis, RabbitMQ, Container Manager & Kafka Explorer moved to plugins
    </h1>
    <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-8 max-w-2xl">
      If one of these tools disappeared from your sidebar after an update, that's expected.
      Nothing is broken. You can install it again as a plugin.
    </p>

    <div class="border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/30 mb-8">
      <p class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3">What changed</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        These four tools used to be built into the app. They now live in a separate repository as
        optional plugins, which keeps the main installer small. You download only what you use.
      </p>
      <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        {movedTools.map((t) => (
          <li class="text-sm">
            <span class="font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">{t.name}</span>
            <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">{t.desc}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/30 mb-8">
      <p class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Your saved connections were not carried over</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        Each plugin keeps its data in its own storage, separate from the app. Old connection details
        aren't moved over, so you'll need to enter them again once after installing the plugin.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/30 mb-10">
      <p class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Everything else is unchanged</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        API Client, Mock Server, Network Tools, the JSON and SQL formatters, JWT Debugger,
        Encode·Hash·Encrypt, and every other <a href={url('/tools')} class="underline hover:text-slate-700 dark:hover:text-slate-300">built-in tool</a>
        still ship with the app. Only the four tools above moved.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a
      href={url('/plugins')}
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 dark:bg-white text-white dark:text-slate-900 text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 transition-colors"
    >
      Reinstall the tools you need →
    </a>
  </div>
</Layout>
